      "weather": "Fine",
      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Terrific race. GURU WARRIOR (2) looked a bit plain last time but had a couple of things against him. Big run fresh then stayed at 1400m for a stakes race, then straight to this journey on soft ground. Was there until late but weakened out of it. Will be much fitter again, has a great record here at the trip, drops in weight and with firmer footing suspect we'll see the real Guru this time. Won't be easy though with plenty of other win chances. GIGGENBACH (6) is a Victorian overdue for a win. The blinkers go on and did finish just ahead of GURU WARRIOR last time. OXFORD BLUE (3) was fourth fresh over a mile in this class in an eye-catching return. Extra trip a plus and excels second-up. CRADLE OF JAZZ (4) is another from the race won by Like A Tiger, finishing runner-up. Light weight and will give a sight again. TYUSIX (5) was a mile winner in easier grade last time and is down in weight and suited by the longer journey now.",
